course: dictionary
lesson: 3919
title: One word, many places: front
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word front has one main idea: first, or ahead of the rest. The front is the part that comes first, and «in front of» someone means just before them or ahead of them.
explain: The front of a thing is the side you see first or the side that faces forward. «The front door» is the door you use first, and «the front page» is the first page you see. In a line, the front is the start of the line.
explain: Front can also be a weather word. A front is where warm and cold air meet. When you meet a new meaning, swap your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Front means the part that is first or ahead of the rest.
fact: In front of means just before or ahead of someone or something.
fact: «In Ohio, a teacher hands Everett a note in front of everyone» means the teacher gives it to him where everyone can see.
fact: «The painter is the rope at the front of a boat» means the rope at the front end, used to tie the boat up.
fact: In weather, a front is where warm and cold air meet.
exercise: «The painter is the rope at the front of a boat.» Where is the painter? | *At the front end of the boat | Floating in the water | Under the seat in the middle | At the back end of the boat
exercise: Which phrase means just before or ahead of someone? | *in front of | far away from | after | under
exercise: «Theatre is a story told live, right in front of you.» What does this tell you about the actors? | *They are really there, close to you | They are behind a wall | They are on a screen far away | They will be filmed later
test: «Clearing the name of the person you blamed, in front of the same people, is part of putting it right.» What does in front of mean here? | Under the table | *Where the same people can see it | Hidden from the people | Long after the people have left
test: In weather, what is a front? | A kind of cold, wet rain | *The place where warm and cold air meet | A window in the sky | A wind blowing from the north
exam: What does front mean in «the front page of the newspaper»? | The page with the weather on it | A page with pictures only | *The first page you see | The last page of the paper
